---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getJobs, formatSpan, currentTitle } from '~/lib/content';

/**
 * The career timeline here is generated from the same `jobs` collection the
 * resume page reads. The prose around it is Phase 3's.
 */
const jobs = await getJobs('site');
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Ali Wallick.">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    Born and raised in Miami, I got interested in games young — young enough that I burned through
    my family's long-distance minutes calling my uncle for advice on <em>Myst</em> at age seven. In high
    school I found the Computational Media program at Georgia Tech and knew immediately it was the right
    fit: computer science and digital media, in equal parts. I spent my time there taking every game development
    class I could find and going to events like Global Game Jam and the Microsoft College Puzzle Challenge,
    and graduated in 2011 with one goal — get into the games industry.
  </p>

  <p>
    That's mostly what the rest of this page is. Fifteen years in, most of it in UI and systems
    engineering: four years at Kaneva going from a new engineer to leading its UI team, a year on a
    much bigger PC shooter at Red 5 Studios, three years shipping casino mobile games at
    MobilityWare — and since 2019, Second Dinner, where I joined as the studio's 11th employee. I
    spent five years on
    <a href="https://marvelsnap.com/credits/">Marvel Snap</a>, which shipped in October 2022, and in
    2024 moved to the studio's next team. Second Dinner has said
    <a
      href="https://www.w4games.com/blog/w4-games-news-1/second-dinner-studios-becomes-a-strategic-investor-in-w4-games-and-plans-to-build-the-largest-game-in-godot-yet-37"
    >
      publicly
    </a> that it's building its next game in Godot; beyond that, it's not mine to talk about yet.
  </p>

  <h2>Where I've worked</h2>
  <ul class="project-list">
    {
      jobs.map((job) => (
        <li>
          <strong>{currentTitle(job)}</strong>, {job.data.company}
          <p class="meta">
            {job.data.location} · {formatSpan(job.data.start, job.data.end)}
          </p>
          {job.data.summary && <p>{job.data.summary}</p>}
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h2>Off the clock</h2>
  <p>
    Most of my free time goes to my family — including my young daughter and our pets — plus games,
    reading, camping, cooking, baking, and crafting, usually some combination of those with friends
    along the way. I'm a longtime science fiction and fantasy fan, in books and on screen, and I
    still make time for game jams and personal projects on the side. When I'm away from the computer
    I gravitate toward hands-on, creative things; costuming has become one of them, including a Best
    Group Costume win at Dragon Con for a <em>Kerbal Space Program</em> cosplay.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
